+integrated R3 with R4/R5/R6 deltas as overridden by ROOT. This module owns current
+invocation authority, exclusive capture/prepare, build transfer, finalize, activation
+and resume. It calls the lower historian/source-proof modules and ordinary content
+validators with explicit reloaded proof bindings. Current State authority is checked
+here, outside the source-proof leaf.
+
+Public API (fixed names/signatures per contract S11):
+  prepare_renewal(root, state_path, renewal_id, intent, manuscript_spec_path,
+                  toolchain_spec_path, executor, recorded_at)
+  finalize_renewal(root, state_path, basis_path, checks_path, semantic_review_path,
+                   visual_review_path, executor, recorded_at)
+  validate_renewal_receipt(root, receipt_path)
+  validate_prepared_renewal_set(root, state_path, set_path)
+  activate_renewal(root, state_path, set_path, reason, executor, recorded_at)
+  resume_renewal_activation(root, state_path, record_path)
+  verify_renewal_history(root, record_path)
+  verify_renewal_rerender_equality(root, basis_path, proof_path)
+  observe_renewal_authority(root, state_path, basis_path)
+
+Entry procedure (binding, root S2): strict no-follow pinned State/config bytes,
+State validated against agent.STATE_SCHEMA before indexing, canonical State path
+derived from exact Profile ref + cfg.state_authority.authoritative_filename (same
+source-root rule as P1 1575-1583; no basename inference), Profile through
+agent._profile_and_source (live-live binding only), pure prePreview/Exception
+window (exact P1 414-429 predicates), then PUBLIC agent.validate_agent_state on
+the same LIVE bytes with no pending argument; pinned bytes rechecked after the
+call. The sole State pointer must select a nonnull versioned record/set/Candidate.
+production.verify_state_basis is NEVER called on renewal history/source/high
+paths (it is a different globally current-pinned API, not a substitute). No
+caller policy enum, no reusable permission result, no synthetic State, no
+verified-dict token, no pending flags.
